# PROJECT: SOLEVERSE — THE NEXT GENERATION OF SNEAKER CULTURE

Act as a senior full-stack developer, UI/UX designer, ecommerce architect, motion designer, and conversion optimization specialist. Build a complete, premium, highly interactive, production-style sneaker ecommerce website named **SOLEVERSE**.

The website should sell trendy Gen Z sneakers, streetwear shoes, chunky sneakers, futuristic runners, retro basketball shoes, skate shoes, minimalist everyday sneakers, platform shoes, and limited-edition drops.

This must be a substantial multi-page ecommerce application with a large product catalog, realistic shopping functionality, responsive layouts, persistent local storage, smooth animations, customer support, order management, and WhatsApp integration.

Do not create just a landing page, a static mockup, or a collection of non-functional buttons. Build the complete frontend experience with functional navigation, product filtering, cart management, checkout validation, order creation, and customer interactions.

## 1. TECHNOLOGY STACK

Use the following technologies:

- Next.js with the App Router.
- React and TypeScript.
- Tailwind CSS for all primary styling.
- Lucide React for icons.
- Framer Motion or Motion for smooth animations and micro-interactions.
- Browser LocalStorage for persistent cart, wishlist, recently viewed products, customer preferences, and demo orders.
- Reusable React components and well-organized project architecture.
- Next.js Image component or an appropriate image-loading solution for product imagery.
- React Context or an equivalent lightweight state-management approach for shared cart, wishlist, and customer state.

Use a compatible current Next.js and Tailwind CSS setup. Ensure all dependencies, imports, routes, and components work together.

Use client components only where browser APIs, event handlers, animations, or interactive state require them. Access LocalStorage safely after client-side mounting to avoid hydration errors.

Do not require a paid API, external database, or secret API key for the basic shopping experience. All essential demo features must work locally.

